   "answer": "Cy Twombly Sr. was a Major League Baseball pitcher who died at age 77 in Savannah, Georgia. The search results do not mention a car accident as the cause of death.",
   "source": "Cy Twombly (baseball) - https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cy_Twombly_(baseball)",
   "excerpt": "Edwin Parker \"Cy\" Twombly Sr. (June 15, 1897 – December 3, 1974) was an American right-handed pitcher in Major League Baseball who appeared in seven games for the 1921 Chicago White Sox. ... He died at age 77 in Savannah, Georgia.",
